    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nToyota Recalls 105,794 Land Cruiser Hybrids in the US for a Fuel Leak It Cannot Explain\n225 photos\nPhoto: Toyota\nToyota Motor North America has a problem it spent around two years trying to understand. It still cannot explain that problem, and that makes this recall all the more interesting. As it happens, a retaining clip on a fuel tube connection can lift, separate the joint, and let gasoline leak. Per TMNA, up to 105,794 examples of the Land Cruiser are being recalled over this concern.\n26V673 is the NHTSA campaign number, whereas Toyota refers to it as 26TA23. Covering model years 2024 through 2027 and production dates from November 29, 2023, to October 1, 2026, the 250-series Land Cruiser population is enormous. Truth be told, it appears to cover all US-market vehicles produced through October 1, 2026.\nToyota's US subsidiary cannot estimate how many examples of the Prado carry the defect because it never found the root cause behind those iffy clips. The resin fuel tube on the fuel tank connects to a main metal fuel tube feeding the turbocharged inline-four mill up front. If the retaining clip on that connector lifts, the joint comes apart, and that's bad news if there's an ignition source nearby.\nToyota Motor North America started hearing about this in 2024. Dealer technicians found the retainer clip lifted or missing on reported vehicles, reseating the connector or swapping the resin tube under warranty. The Japanese manufacturer then went looking for a manufacturing-related root cause, but came up empty.\nCCTV footage from the factory showed the clip perfectly seated at the time of assembly, and production records showed no process deviation or rework. Even supplier sampling data confirmed dimensions within Toyota's specifications. FTS Co. is the supplier in question, and its investigation involved recovered tubes from the US and overseas markets.\nPhoto: Toyota The supplier's investigation found markings on the connectors consistent with the tube being pulled apart while the retainer clip sat in an unlocked state, pointing to the clip being lifted after the subject population left the factory. TMNA then tried to break the connection, performing pull tests on newly manufactured tubes with properly seated clips.\nSaid testing showed the connector housing failing before any disconnect. Vibration and pressure tests followed suit, along with vibration and pressure runs. All failed to separate a properly installed joint. Given the aforementioned, Toyota 's safety boffins then drove Prados through standing water at various depths and speeds.\nOnly when the clip was left deliberately unseated did the connection let go. This scenario leads to a joint failure, which eventually results in the fuel pump shutting off while driving. When that happens, the Land Cruiser 250-series hybrid drops into electric mode with reduced power.\nAt the beginning of October 2026, the automaker was aware of 23 field technical reports and 64 warranty claims in the US market. The fix comes in the form of a supplemental clamp to keep the joint from separating. If the dealer inspection calls for it, the resin fuel tube may be replaced at no charge to affected customers.\nDealers were notified on October 14, while customer letters are expected to be mailed between November 29 and December 13. In the meantime, the most practical move is to get in touch with your dealer or perform a VIN check on Toyota's consumer website.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nToyota toyota land cruiser recall US SUV\nDownload: Toyota Land Cruiser fuel leak recall (PDF)\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT The $18,995 Ford Custom Garage Bronco ORV Package Ticks All the Right Off-Road Boxes",
